Here? In front of god and everybody?	在這裡？當著眾人與神明之前？
It is ready upon your arm.	它已備妥，就在你臂上。
The sweet heady smell of the rose reminds you, inevitably, of Gwenhyver.	玫瑰那濃郁香甜的氣息，讓你不由自主地想起昆海兒。
What is it you wish to do instead?	那麼你想改做什麼？
This is not the Chapel of the Two Gods. Here, you can only hope that whatever god or goddess is listening will heed your prayers.	此處並非雙神神殿。在這裡，你只能盼望，不論是哪位神祇正聽著，都願垂聽你的禱告。
A mysterious request. Try to rephrase it more clearly.	這是個令人費解的要求，試著換個更清楚的說法。
That is rather vague.  Which animal?	這話說得太籠統了。是哪種動物？
There are many knights in the world. You must name the one for which you seek.	世上騎士眾多，你得說出你所尋之人的姓名。
What difficulty:	難度：
The joust will continue until either you or I have been unhorsed three times. Let it begin!	這場馬上長槍比武，將持續到你我任一方被擊落馬下三次為止。開始吧！
You have vanquished the Black Knight, King Arthur!	你已擊敗黑武士，亞瑟王！
You have struck your first successful blow against the Black Knight!	你已首次成功擊中黑武士！
You have unhorsed the Black Knight for the second time! Once more and you have won!	你已第二次將黑武士擊落馬下！再一次，你便獲勝了！
Alas! All Camelot will grieve to hear that valiant King Arthur was slain by the Black Knight.	唉！全肯萊特聞知驍勇的亞瑟王死於黑武士之手，無不哀慟。
The Black Knight has unhorsed you for the first time, Arthur. Make it the last!	黑武士已首次將你擊落馬下，亞瑟。務必讓這是最後一次！
Beware! The Black Knight has struck a second telling blow against you.	當心！黑武士已對你造成第二次重擊。
OW!	哎唷！
Deal with the Mad Monk and his illusions! Then you will have time to look around.	先解決瘋僧侶與他的幻術！之後你才有時間四處查看。
Like a mad dog, he has been destroyed.  Tragic, but necessary.	他如瘋狗一般，已遭剷除。可悲，卻是不得不然。
Arthur, beware!  Two of these monks are illusions, but one is deadly!	亞瑟，當心！這些僧侶中有兩個是幻影，但有一個是致命的！
Kill!  Kill!  Kill!	殺！殺！殺！
One must be off a horse to get on a horse.	人得先下馬，才能上馬。
Your warhorse is trained to be mounted from the left side.	你的戰馬受過訓練，習慣從左側上馬。
You have only begun your journey. You can surely stay in your saddle longer than this.	你的旅程才剛開始。你當然能在馬鞍上撐得比這更久。
There are very few places in the forest where that would be either safe or advisable.  This is not one of them.	這片森林裡，既安全又適宜這麼做的地方少之又少。此處並非其中之一。
This is no time to wander about on foot. Do get on with your mission.	此刻不是徒步閒晃的時候。快去完成你的使命。
Being a superb rider, you do not carry one.	身為出色的騎手，你並未攜帶這東西。
Not now.  You have places to go.	現在不行，你還有地方要去。
Your horse is not cold, Arthur.	你的坐騎並不冷，亞瑟。
You already have the reins.	韁繩已經在你手上了。
Mount your horse first, Arthur.	先上馬吧，亞瑟。
You need not tie a trained warhorse.	訓練有素的戰馬，不必拴繫。
He looks much the same as last time you looked at him.	他的模樣，和你上次看他時沒什麼兩樣。
Your horse is built for power, stamina and solidity to carry you with armor and weaponry into battle.  This does not make him a very good jumper.	你的坐騎生來力大、耐久、體格堅實，足以馱著全副武裝的你上陣殺敵，卻不擅長跳躍。
Do you suffer from the delusion that you are on a horse?	你是不是有種錯覺，以為自己正騎在馬上？
One must generally be on a horse to do that.	一般來說，得先騎在馬上才能這麼做。
It would be best to go at a pace the mule can match.	最好放慢腳步，配合騾子能跟上的速度。
Trust the instincts of your well-trained steed.  He knows when to hurry and when to tread with care.	相信你那匹訓練有素的坐騎的本能，牠明白何時該加快腳步、何時該小心慢行。
There will be time enough for that later.	之後有的是時間做這件事。
Jabir likes not the flash of your steel.	賈比耳不喜你鋼刃出鞘的寒光。
Jabir likes not the sound of your steel being drawn.	賈比耳不喜你拔劍出鞘的聲響。
You have set Jabir to his heels.  Let us hope that will be the last of him.  You have no strength to spare for chasing him.	你已把賈比耳嚇得拔腿逃竄。但願此後不會再見到他。你已無餘力去追捕他。
Your mule carries your pack containing extra clothes, water and provisions.	你的騾子馱著行囊，裡頭裝著替換衣物、飲水與糧食。
That is best left where it is.	那東西還是留在原處的好。
For what purpose?	為了什麼目的？
What you are wearing will do for now.	你目前身上穿的，暫時夠用了。
The frost and ice chill the soul more than the body.	霜雪凍的不只是身軀，更是靈魂。
It is not THAT cold.	還沒冷到那個地步。
You are carrying quite enough as it is.  That is why you have a pack mule.	你身上背的已經夠多了，這正是你有一頭馱騾的緣故。
The mule does not need the blanket, nor do you need a blanket that smells like a mule.	騾子不需要這條毯子，你也不需要一條滿是騾子氣味的毯子。
You may talk to your mule all you like, Arthur, as long as you do not expect her to talk back.	你儘管對著騾子說話，亞瑟，只要別指望她會回話就好。
She already carries the pack and you have your horse.	她已經馱著行囊了，而你有自己的坐騎。
The weight of the pack is enough.  Your own two feet will serve to carry you.	行囊的重量已經夠了，靠你自己的雙腳走就行。
You must be on your guard here.  Best to wait until you are free of the forest to take your ease.	此處你必須保持戒備。最好等離開這片森林後，再放鬆歇息。
You did that during your journey here.	你在來此的路上已經做過這件事了。
Time enough for that later.  135 For now, think only of your mission.	之後有的是時間做這件事。135 眼下，你只需想著你的使命。
The pack washed overboard in the storm, remember?	還記得嗎？那個行囊在風暴中被沖落海裡了。
No need.  She will follow you as usual.	不必，她會照常跟著你。
A mule is not for riding.  Your own two feet will serve to carry you.	騾子不是用來騎的，靠你自己的雙腳走就行。
Arthur! The mule is an innocent animal and should be valued. Do try to show some sense.	亞瑟！騾子是無辜的牲畜，理應受到珍視。拿出點分寸來。
Your mule does not need to be tied.	你的騾子不需要拴繫。
It is a book of knowledge which should be in your possession already. It looks like this and it is vital that you have it.	這是一本你早該持有的知識之書，模樣便是如此，你務必要隨身攜帶。
The Message of the Rose is written in your liber ex doctrina.	玫瑰箴言，寫在你的《Liber ex Doctrina》裡。
Clearly he is not here.	他顯然不在此處。
The Liber ex Doctrina looks like this. I sincerely hope you have it with you.	《Liber ex Doctrina》模樣便是如此，衷心盼望你有隨身攜帶。
You have worn these sturdy leather boots on many journeys. They will last quite a while yet.	這雙結實的皮靴，你已穿著走過許多路程，還能再撐上一段時日。
It's nice armor, isn't it?	這副鎧甲不錯吧？
I am only with you in spirit, but that should be enough.	我只能以心神與你同在，但那應該就夠了。
That is on the mule, wherever she is.	那東西在騾子身上，不論她此刻在哪裡。
I see nothing that is significant to your mission.	我看不出這與你的使命有何干係。
That would solve nothing.	那樣做無濟於事。
What an abysmally foolish idea.	這主意愚蠢至極。
Unnecessary violence is a stain upon the soul.	不必要的暴力，是靈魂上的污點。
You had better don sword and armour first.	你最好先佩劍披甲。
I have nothing special to tell you now.	此刻我沒有什麼特別的話要告訴你。
I have no special knowledge to help you here.	在這件事上，我沒有特別的見識能幫上你。
I am unable to help more at this time.	此刻我無法再多幫你什麼了。
That would avail you nothing.	那對你毫無助益。
At the moment, I know no more than you of his fate.	此刻，他的命運我所知並不比你多。
I would gladly tell you more if I had the knowledge.	若我知道得更多，必然樂意告訴你。
I can tell you nothing relevant at the moment.	此刻我沒有任何相關的事能告訴你。
Aye, that is the purpose of your mission.	正是，那正是你此行的目的。
I do not see how you can, unless you know something I do not.	我看不出你能如何辦到，除非你知道某些我不知道的事。
Obtain only what you need. Your burdens are already great.	只取你所需之物，你肩上的負擔已經夠重了。
This is no time for the vulgar pursuit of money.	此刻不是追逐俗世錢財的時候。
That is not for sale.	那東西不賣。
Search what?	搜什麼？
There is nothing of interest.	沒有什麼值得注意的東西。
I would not look up into the blindingly bright sky too often, if I were you.	換作是我，不會太常抬頭直視那刺目的天空。
In your armour?  Without ladder or scaling gear?  Do not be absurd.	穿著這身鎧甲？又沒有梯子或攀爬用具？休得荒唐。
The walls are far too high for that.	這牆太高了，辦不到。
I can see no purpose in that.	我看不出這麼做有什麼意義。
You would not enjoy that.  Trust me.	你不會喜歡那種滋味的，相信我。
Draw your sword only when absolutely necessary, or you may attract attention you do not want.  Remember the captain's warning.	非到萬不得已，切莫拔劍，否則恐招來你不樂見的注目。記住那位船長的警告。
Let us pray that the end of your mission will lie within these walls.	讓我們祈禱，你此行的終點就在這城牆之內。
You cannot actually see much of the city from outside the walls.	站在城牆之外，你其實看不清這座城市多少樣貌。
At least you know what to expect this time.	至少這一回，你已知道會遇到什麼。
Let us hope that other gates will not be as inhospitable as the one you passed.	但願其他城門不會像你剛經過的那道一樣難以親近。
The narrow path around the walls of Jerusalem is hard packed soil.  It drops off quite steeply, so be careful.	耶路撒冷城牆外那條窄路，是踩得結實的泥土地，坡度頗陡，務必小心。
The Zion Gate is a small gate in the south wall of Jerusalem.	錫安城門是耶路撒冷南牆上的一道小城門。
The Jaffa Gate is the main gate in the western wall of Jerusalem.	賈法城門是耶路撒冷西牆上的主城門。
Some of the spiny plants are Aloe Vera.  The others are some Eastern desert varieties unknown to me.	這些帶刺的植物，有些是蘆薈，其餘則是我所不識的東方沙漠品種。
Trees do not seem to fare well around here.  I see nothing but shrubs.	這一帶樹木似乎長得不好，我看到的盡是灌木叢。
Aloe Vera is originally from Africa.  The leaves have a bitter, astringent juice within.	蘆薈原產自非洲，葉片中含有苦澀的汁液。
My that IS a steep drop.	哎呀，這坡可真陡。
There is no cause to swear at me, Arthur.  It was your own clumsiness that caused it.	沒理由衝著我咒罵，亞瑟，這是你自己笨手笨腳造成的。
Now pick yourself up, dust yourself off, and we shall start all over again.	現在起身，拍拍身上塵土，我們從頭再來一次。
The whirlwind of rose petals will guide and protect you, but only if you stay within it.	玫瑰花瓣的旋風會指引並護佑你，但唯有你留在其中方能生效。
The petals disperse in an icy wind. You are no longer protected by its spell of guidance.	花瓣在寒風中四散消逝。你已不再受那指引法術的護佑。
Rather than waste your time in fruitless endeavors, I advise you to simply avoid the mummies and the urns and concentrate upon your task -- finding a way out of here.	與其把時間浪費在徒勞無功之事上，我勸你乾脆避開木乃伊與陶甕，專心於你的任務——找到離開此處的路。
The rats are too quick and can hide too easily from your sword. You are wasting precious time, Arthur.	這些老鼠動作太快，輕易便能躲過你的劍。你在浪費寶貴的時間，亞瑟。
The elixir is gone and I did not keep track of where you dropped the empty vial.	解藥已經用盡，你把空瓶丟在哪裡，我也沒留意。
I am quite disoriented in these catacombs. You could be facing in any direction, for all I can tell.	在這地下墓窖裡，我完全辨不清方向。就我所知，你此刻可能面朝任何一方。
The red eyes of a poisonous rat glare back at you.	一隻毒鼠赤紅的雙眼，正回瞪著你。
There is a plenty of dust and rat droppings.	這裡滿是塵土與鼠糞。
The lethal rats of the catacombs lurk behind these mummies.	墓窖裡致命的老鼠，就潛伏在這些木乃伊後方。
There is a vaulted stone ceiling.	這裡有一座拱形的石頂。
The floor is made of cold, cold stone.	地板是由冰冷、冰冷的石頭鋪成的。
The poisonous rats are everywhere, but seem to favor the mummies and urns. Best to stay clear of them.	毒鼠四處都是，但似乎特別偏好木乃伊與陶甕一帶。最好離牠們遠一點。
Remember the hierophant's warning: one bite means a slow but certain death. To be bitten more than once, will hasten that terrible fate.	記住祭司的警告：被咬一口，便是緩慢卻必然的死亡；若不止一次被咬，那可怕的命運將提前降臨。
The niches hold the mummies, as you can clearly see.	壁龕裡安放著木乃伊，這你看得很清楚。
The doorways are quite low and show how thick the walls are between the rooms.	這些門道相當低矮，正顯出房間之間牆壁的厚實。
A spell of warding is one which repels evil spirits or creatures.	防護法術，是能驅退邪靈或邪祟生物的法術。
I suppose it could be hidden in these catacombs. You must be alert to any possibility.	我猜想它或許就藏在這片墓窖之中，你得對任何可能保持警覺。
You let him die, Arthur. Your soul will never be cleansed of this sin.	你任由他死去，亞瑟。你的靈魂將永遠洗刷不去這樁罪孽。
So close was he to death, that it may take some time for the elixir to work. Your only chance is to find the Grail so that it may heal you.	他已如此接近死亡，解藥恐怕得花上一段時間才能見效。你唯一的機會，是尋得聖杯，讓聖杯治癒你。
Though you have not found him, he may yet be in some undiscovered chamber.	雖然你尚未尋獲他，他或許仍在某個未被發現的密室之中。
If you seek such knowledge, consult your Liber ex Doctrina.	若你尋求這樣的知識，請查閱你的《Liber ex Doctrina》。
There is no mural here.	此處沒有壁畫。
Gnostic means "knowledge." It refers to secretive Christian cults who seek after heavenly knowledge, disdain all matters of the flesh, and worship Sophia, the Great Mother of all wisdom.	「諾斯替」（Gnostic）意為「知識」，指的是那些追求天啟知識、鄙棄一切肉身之事、崇奉索菲亞──萬智之大母的秘密基督教教派。